            "paragraph": "A compromise was made with black carbon (BC), the most important tracer of combustion sources in order to achieve better global coverage. Results from aethalometer (Hansen et al., 1982) and other photometric methods (Andreae et al., 1983; Bond et al., 1999; Heintzenberg, 1982; Heintzenberg, 1988) were accepted even though there are calibration discrepancies between these methods (Heintzenberg et al., 1997).",
